<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!--
      The app's own theme, and it exists for exactly one reason: to drop the
      platform ActionBar.

      The manifest asked for Theme.DeviceDefault.DayNight, whose ActionBar drew
      a full bar showing nothing but the android:label ("CardEngine") above
      every screen. The Creator already draws its own CgTopBar underneath it,
      and the Player draws its own toolbar row, so that bar was duplicated
      chrome everywhere and, on the play surface, a band of screen the lanes
      could have had.

      Written as a local style rather than switching the manifest to a
      framework NoActionBar variant, because the framework has no
      DayNight.NoActionBar: the DayNight and NoActionBar axes do not cross in
      android:style. Inheriting DayNight and turning the bar off keeps the
      automatic light/dark behaviour that res/values-night relies on.
    -->
    <style name="CardEngineTheme" parent="@android:style/Theme.DeviceDefault.DayNight">
        <item name="android:windowActionBar">false</item>
        <item name="android:windowNoTitle">true</item>
    </style>
</resources>
